&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Development Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Custodian and CRM Integrations&lt;/strong&gt; Team!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team’s mission is to enable clients and partners to integrate with Addepar. Our cross-functional team designs, develops and operates automated workflows between Addepar and 3rd party systems. We aim to serve a variety of needs from slick no-code UI options, to more complex workflows built on top of our &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.addepar.com&quot;&gt;APIs&lt;/a&gt;. Take a look at our &lt;a href=&quot;https://integrations.addepar.com&quot;&gt;Integration Center&lt;/a&gt; to see some of the existing integrations!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who will build an inclusive team culture, empower engineers to succeed and cultivate an environment that creates high-quality engineering processes and product delivery. You’ll work closely with product and design to deliver great products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team works primarily with Java, making use of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://temporal.io/&quot;&gt;Temporal&lt;/a&gt; durable execution engine to orchestrate our integration workflows. We also work on projects that require the use of Apex (proprietary Salesforce language), Javascript (Ember and LWC frameworks) and Python.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
